  "description": "There are only a few simple steps to a perfect watermelon, feta, and mint salad. This easy recipe lays them out.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Up to 4 ounces (1 quart) arugula leaves (optional; see note)\n\nNotes: This dish greatly depends on the quality of the feta. If you have options at your supermarket, look for true Greek or Bulgarian sheep's milk feta, which tends to be creamier and tangier than domestic cow's-milk versions.\nTo make this salad more substantial, add arugula.",
